    },
    "body": "Balanced source-only geometric compiler training now crosses frames with arbitrary values and retains nonwrite controls. Six actual fits across three head seeds improve development store and native bank replies, while fresh source compilation remains0/32. The old64-row supplied-record curriculum measured consumption, not retrieval; its scope is documented in the Claude a–e audit.\n\nAn exact native score probe reproduces7,560 retained predictions across six fits/five checkpoints. It separates raw action/role heads from span-fallback final actions and exposes contradictory supervision on unused query/NONE span branches: conditioning on labelled writes removes96/100 local conflicts, leaving4 genuine boundary ambiguities. The next repair is conditional span learning, preserving all act/role and false-write controls. No runtime predictor change or fresh success claim is introduced here.\n\nValidation:8 original curriculum tests/release and six fits atcc007092;9 library+2 probe+8 curriculum tests/release and six zero-update replays at51be10a0. Reviewed HEAD 0968bc0feee19fa29fec4fbeccb97b29ad581a28 changes only documentation since51be10a0; numerical source bytes are identical. Independent saved-artifact audits admit7,560rows/8,938,809checks, with explicit native/BPE/backward/BLAKE3 exclusions. Claim wording and whitespace checks pass. Actual CPU-only Linux execution/cost, source/executable/artifact identities, positives/negatives/interruption and verified iCloud retention are in docs/evidence. Metal unavailable; no GPU. GitHub compatibility acknowledgements do not run tests.\n\nReferences #820, #1552. Shared GroundedSession files unchanged. General chat, reasoning and laptop energy remain unqualified.\n",
